{
  "slug": "attune-lite",
  "name": "Attune Lite",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Six developer workflow commands for Claude Code: code review, security audit, test generation, test fixing, bug prediction, and documentation generation.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills** and **6 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `bug-predict` (Use when the user asks to predict bugs, find risky code, or assess code risk), `code-review` (Use when the user asks for a code review, wants feedback on code quality, or mentions reviewing code…), `doc-gen` (Use when the user asks to generate documentation, write a README, document an API, or audit existing docs), `security-audit` (Use when the user asks for a security audit, vulnerability scan, or security review), `smart-test` (Use when the user asks to generate tests, find test gaps, audit test coverage, or improve testing)\n- **Commands** (6): `bug-predict` (Predict likely bug locations based on code patterns and complexity), `code-review` (Run a multi-pass code review (security, quality, performance, architecture)), `doc-gen` (Generate documentation from source code), `fix-test` (Auto-diagnose and fix your last failed tests), `security-audit` (Run a security audit with vulnerability scanning and remediation planning), `smart-test` (Find test gaps and generate tests for uncovered code)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install attune-lite@claude-community` from `Smart-AI-Memory/attune-lite`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
